  "Content": {
    "$Comment": "Phase 4 (AT_Ice_King_Air_Enraged) extra combat behaviour, plugged into the vanilla Template_Flying_Aggressive hook CombatAdditionalBehaviorComponent; it runs before the template's own ranged attack (the normal ice ray). A flying template has no CAE, so the extra attacks go on timers here. 1) Health regen off once. 2) Freezing ray every 6 s (first after 3 s) when the target is within 24 blocks in sight: And(Target, Timer) + HeadMotion Aim + Attack, the pattern of vanilla Template_Dungeon_Goblin_Lobber's enraged lane. The Attack action starts nothing while another attack runs, so it never overlaps the normal ray. 3) Every 15 s (first after 6 s), while at most 9 Gunters are within 30 blocks, summon 3 (12 at most); same pattern as Component_AT_Ice_King_Air_Combat. 2026-10-21: circles around the player (AT_CIRCLE, radius 13) instead of hovering over his head. 2026-10-21 (playtest: harder in the rage phase): every HeadMotion Aim here has Deflection true, so he aims where the player WILL be (HeadMotionAim: target velocity in the ballistic solution). It only works for attacks with an AimingReference projectile (the ice ray, the freezing ray); bolts without one (Zap, burst) and the beam still aim at where the player is.",
    "Continue": true,
    "Sensor": {
      "Type": "Any"
    },
    "Instructions": [
      {
        "$Comment": "2026-10-21: phase-change animation (AT_Ice_King model set PhaseChange, Status slot) once when he reaches combat in this role. The flying template's Alerted state plays a fixed Alerted animation, so the air roles shorten AlertedTime and this one plays right after it.",
        "Continue": true,
        "Sensor": {
          "Type": "Any",
          "Once": true
        },
        "Actions": [
          {
            "Type": "PlayAnimation",
            "Slot": "Status",
            "Animation": "PhaseChange"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "$Comment": "Ice shield hit counter (2026-10-21: the shield breaks after 5 s or 5 hits): a hit taken while AT_Ice_King_Ice_Shield is on moves the invisible counter up one step (Damage sensor: true only on the tick he took damage, NPCEntity.clearDamageData every tick; hits from his own group do not count). Highest step first, so one hit moves exactly one step. 5th hit: AT_Ice_King_Shield_Broken, and AT_Ice_King_Ice_Shield bursts. Continue, nothing else is stopped.",
        "Continue": true,
